## ❓ FAQ

<details>
<summary><b>Chinese characters show as boxes (□□□)</b></summary>

Nothing — on Windows/macOS CJK fonts are pre-installed and auto-detected. On Linux: `sudo apt install fonts-noto-cjk`. The library scans for installed CJK fonts (SimHei, Microsoft YaHei, PingFang, Noto Sans CJK…) at import and applies them automatically.
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>How do I save a vector PDF for submission?</b></summary>

```python
fig = plot(..., )
fig.savefig('figure.pdf')          # or .svg / .eps
```
PDF/SVG are vector formats and scale to any size without pixelation.
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>My chart type name is "unknown"</b></summary>

Typos return close-match suggestions: `plot(..., type='barr')` → *Unknown chart type 'barr'. Did you mean: 'bar', 'barh', 'bullet'?* Run `mmv types` or `list_chart_types()` for the full list (190+ aliases).
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Can I tweak the figure after plot() returns it?</b></summary>

Yes — it's a normal matplotlib Figure. `ax = fig.axes[0]`, then use any matplotlib API.
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Does it work in Jupyter?</b></summary>

Yes. `%matplotlib inline` is all you need; figures render as cell output.
</details>

